docs/projects/V1-IMPLEMENTATION.md:19:T01 is the v0.9 release-path priority. Its merge permits the bot to regenerate the release PR; fresh decision/source agreement and passing CI must precede any separately authorized merge/publication. Other lanes do not automatically become v0.9 release requirements. Existing-contract fixes can run while the architectural decisions below are being reviewed.
docs/projects/V1-IMPLEMENTATION.md:28:| Workflow integration | T10 intent-selected outputs → T10-NAPI lifecycle ownership | No unrelated builds or duplicate publication authority; native preparation/packing still works |
docs/projects/V1-IMPLEMENTATION.md:33:## D01: decisions needed before model implementation
docs/projects/V1-IMPLEMENTATION.md:42:| Wire compatibility | Preserve existing string versions where context suffices; version documents whose owner/effect/output semantics change | Enumerate decision/intent/manifest/envelope/receipt readers, accepted old versions, stale decisions and old-intent rerun support; reject unsupported migration explicitly |
docs/projects/V1-IMPLEMENTATION.md:43:| Maturin | First support Cargo-owned `dynamic = ["version"]` and inherited Cargo authority with native Python mapping | Specify static co-located metadata behavior, precedence, unsupported mappings/backends and built wheel/sdist checks; do not force equal numeric strings into one grammar |
docs/projects/V1-IMPLEMENTATION.md:45:| Registry file set | Declare selected outputs before build; bind exact trusted filenames/digests after build without mutating sealed intent | Choose per-file effects or an aggregate operation with explicit partial-state proof; define how build inventory is covered by the existing envelope and how local retries retain original bytes |
docs/projects/V1-IMPLEMENTATION.md:49:D01 records testable contracts in the proposed architecture/ADR and PR packets. Area specs remain current-behavior documents: amend them on each implementation branch with the behavior, and review/hash-bind that contract before a gated implementation handoff. ADR 12 stays proposed until owner acceptance and the implementing merge. No single approved future delta spec currently exists, so the portfolio JSON intentionally has no `linked_spec` or fabricated `spec_hash`; affected criterion mappings are not coverage of all 220 existing criteria.
docs/projects/V1-IMPLEMENTATION.md:77:Plugins guide reasoning and evidence; they do not themselves provide isolated worktrees, a branch scheduler or authorization. Final synthesis, interface decisions and binding readiness stay with the coordinator. Sentinel must report pending/unverifiable evidence rather than converting a targeted test into a whole-release pass.
docs/projects/V1-IMPLEMENTATION.md:102:| `Manifest` / `ManifestIdentity` / `VersionSource` | `CargoToml`, `PackageJson`, `PyprojectToml`; `read_identity`; live base-version and historical blob readers | T03-HISTORY and T07 migrate all reached readers/editors, including writers and snapshots; preserve native parsing and format rules |
docs/projects/V1-IMPLEMENTATION.md:107:| Immutable release wires | Decision, input snapshot, intent, artifact manifest, envelope, receipt, schemas; CLI file/stdout producers and action scripts | T02 inventory; D01 fixes compatibility; T08/T09 migrate producers/consumers, including CLI registry-only inventory acceptance/envelope sealing and local build preparation |
docs/projects/V1-IMPLEMENTATION.md:123:| Native versions/history | Stable Python decisions and pre-state; root/inherited Cargo authority; old schemas and tamper negatives |
docs/projects/V1-IMPLEMENTATION.md:125:| Version interruption | Tracked/untracked input; late refresh/staging/decision failures; no double bump, false success or unrelated edits |
docs/projects/V1-IMPLEMENTATION.md:134:- Included sibling checks: dry-run permit entry boundaries (T05/T08), alternate group-constructor conflict enforcement (T06), redacted indeterminate provider diagnostics (T08), and receipt attempt-scope wording (T12). If a reachable fix is outside its task's file boundary, record a follow-up rather than silently omit it.
docs/projects/V1-IMPLEMENTATION.md:135:- Owner decisions, not invented merge gates: workspace-wide discarded-source-error enforcement, extra npm JSON-layout preservation, stronger release-commit producer provenance, mandatory explicit registry kind and napi output attestation, private Python/HTML support, npm channels, universal registry checksums and wrapper bump severity.
