docs/projects/V1-IMPLEMENTATION.md:49:D01 records testable contracts in the proposed architecture/ADR and PR packets. Area specs remain current-behavior documents: amend them on each implementation branch with the behavior, and review/hash-bind that contract before a gated implementation handoff. ADR 12 stays proposed until owner acceptance and the implementing merge. No single approved future delta spec currently exists, so the portfolio JSON intentionally has no `linked_spec` or fabricated `spec_hash`; affected criterion mappings are not coverage of all 220 existing criteria.
docs/projects/V1-IMPLEMENTATION.md:77:Plugins guide reasoning and evidence; they do not themselves provide isolated worktrees, a branch scheduler or authorization. Final synthesis, interface decisions and binding readiness stay with the coordinator. Sentinel must report pending/unverifiable evidence rather than converting a targeted test into a whole-release pass.
